preConditionHook:
// HOLD THE WIDE STRUCTURAL STOP WHILE THE TREND HAS NOT ONCE CLOSED ON THE WRONG
// SIDE OF THE MOVING AVERAGE. Only after the first such close does the bar-by-bar
// trail arm, and from that point a close beyond the PRIOR bar's extreme takes the
// trade off.
//
// Same recast as TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold: R12-12 states a GATE ("do not
// use a tight stop while there have been no closes below the moving average"),
// and the pane system cannot express one exit conditioning another, so it is
// carried as a single armed trail. Brooks scopes the scan to "since the current
// leg began"; anchored here to SINCE ENTRY, which is mechanizable and avoids the
// leg-definition dependency. The source's minBars = 10 is an artifact of the
// chart example, not a stated condition, and is dropped.
//
// Not BreakevenStopAfterEmaHoldingRun, which counts N consecutive closes HOLDING
// on the right side of the average and arms a BREAKEVEN stop: that arms while
// the trade is going well, this arms on the first close going wrong, and the two
// arm on disjoint bars.
//
// THE FLAGS ARE PER POSITION, reset on ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0 -- VERIFIED as 0
// on the fill bar and as restarting through a reversal, which a
// ctx.MarketPosition() == 0 reset would miss. While flat the reset simply
// repeats; the fill bar itself can set the flag.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls. MEASURED
// (EL_XAverage_Probe.txt, @OJ 240min) bit-identical to the plain XAverage
// built-in at a fixed length. SEED is the PRICE on the study's first calculated
// bar (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1), not a length-term simple average; the recurrence
// is ONE statement in EL's own form, x + sf*(p - x), never sf*p + (1-sf)*x, which
// separates on 67% of bars past 100. NO WARM-UP HOLE: do not add a CurrentBar()
// guard returning 0. An EMA never forgets its seed, so the seed bar is part of
// the specification and moves with Max Bars Back and the chart start. emaLength
// MAY BE OPTIMIZED: the wrapper recomputes SF on a length change and carries its
// state (MEASURED 2026-09-17). Only the CURRENT value is read; no lagged read, so
// no mirrored ring buffer and no first-k-bars guard is needed.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// stopOffsetTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), into a local.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 1 (the EMA itself is recursive state, not a window).
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    brokenLong = false;
    brokenShort = false;
}
if (el_lt(close[0], emaVal)) brokenLong = true;
if (el_gt(close[0], emaVal)) brokenShort = true;
